hi my name is Jeff wall  j-e-f-f-w-a-l-l I'm a sergeant with the  north Las Vegas Police Department here  to tell you about an officer-involved  shooting that happened tonight September  24th 2022. at about 10 14 PM officers  were dispatched to the 4300 block of  westmere Avenue near Grand Teton and  Aviary way  caller reported that a unknown man was  in the backyard of a house with a long  metal pole and he attempt appeared to be  attempting to break into the house  the caller confronted the man  who asked him do you want to die  the caller reported that the man  appeared to be either intoxicated or  high on drugs  when officers arrived at about 10 17 PM  they located the man and he was armed  with a rifle at about 10 30 PM officers  reported that shots had been fired  the man had been shot at least one time  medical personnel were called  immediately and officers rendered  life-saving efforts  and the man was transported to UMC  trauma where he was pronounced deceased  no other persons were injured during  this shooting  the identity of the person deceased  would be released by The Clark County  coroner's office after proper  notifications next of kin  and the identity of the officer involved  will be released by the department after  48 hours pursuant to our department  policy procedure
 

